From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:13:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools: the seccomp filter of the BD-J server

hades_bdj_sandbox_enter() is what the server of the isolated BD-J service
(hades-bdj-host) calls first, before it opens anything of the disc and
before any JVM exists. LibreELEC builds systemd without seccomp, so the
service's own SystemCallFilter= and the other seccomp options would do
nothing; the server installs the filter itself (libseccomp), for every
thread the JVM will start (TSYNC), and then checks from the kernel that the
process is isolated (bdj_sandbox_check()). Any failure: the server exits
without opening the disc.

A list of refusals over a default that allows, not an allow list: what a
JVM calls changes with the JVM, its collectors and glibc, and a call
missing from an allow list would break the menus where nobody looked.
Refused with EPERM: other processes (ptrace, process_vm_*, pidfd_getfd,
kcmp, process_madvise, move_pages, migrate_pages), namespaces, mounts and
roots (unshare, setns, the mount family, chroot, pivot_root; clone with a
namespace flag; clone3 gets ENOSYS, so glibc falls back to clone), new
programs (execve, execveat), kernel interfaces a confined process does not
need (bpf, perf_event_open, userfaultfd, io_uring, keys, handles,
fanotify, syslog...), the machine (modules, kexec, reboot, swap, clocks,
I/O ports, host names), personality() other than the default; sockets of
any family but AF_UNIX get EAFNOSUPPORT (with BD-Live, AF_INET and AF_INET6
too). A system call of another architecture (i386, x32) ends the process.
A refused unshare(0) afterwards shows that this filter, not merely some
filter, is in force.

Measured in the service on the build host (systemd 259), with a test
program after this call: each of those calls refused as said, threads,
anonymous executable memory and AF_UNIX sockets work, an i386 and an x32
call end the process (SIGSYS). A JVM (OpenJDK 8, 17, 21 and 26) runs BD-J
under it.
---
 src/tools/hades_bdj_sandbox.c | 217 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/tools/hades_bdj_sandbox.h |  43 +++++++
 2 files changed, 260 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/tools/hades_bdj_sandbox.c
 create mode 100644 src/tools/hades_bdj_sandbox.h

